{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550103-vicissitude-questions","id":1550103,"title":"Vicissitude Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-13T20:04:14-07:00","id":1550103,"title":"Vicissitude Questions","content":"Hello, I will be playing my first fiend soon. I have experience playing gangrel, and toreador so I understand animalism and auspex pretty well. Vicissitude is more open though so I was looking for some tips and tricks to bring into the future games. Thanks. For example what can be done with vicissitude to the vampires body, can you create working wings, hidden popout weapons, a bone gun out of your arm ect. Can you create armor for yourself and how much and at what cost. Can you make permanent items out of flesh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","user":"Carsusbloodking","date":". 04-14-2025, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28506-carsusbloodking","name":"Carsusbloodking","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T23:18:28-07:00","id":1550104,"title":"","content":"What are your questions? <br /> &quot;Tips and tricks&quot; is a very broad term, thus similarly the answer, the best tips and trick : be creative<br /> But if you narrow a bit down with questions or examples I'm sure plenty of people are willing to help you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-14T07:24:08-07:00","id":1550111,"title":"","content":"One way to use Vicissitude is as a way to justify your vampire being able to acquire Physical Merits that they did not initially possess. That opens up a lot os possibilities without having to stray too far from pre-existing crunch.<br /> <br /> Overall, Vicissitude is one of those tricky Disciplines where a lot of its potential is going to depend on what your Storyteller is willing to permit. The options listed in the actual rules are not nearly as broad as what it is capable of in the lore.<br /> <br /> One particular limit to consider is that you cannot add new biomass without an Elder-level power, Graft Life to Life. There might be a bit of wiggle room there, but you're mostly stuck working with the meat and bone that's already present.<br /> <br /> So, to use the examples you provided, crafting wings would require you to &quot;hollow out&quot; other parts of your body for the necessary flesh and bone, which may leave the recipient more frail than they had been previously.<br /> <br /> A &quot;bone gun&quot; would be quite limited because your Tzimisce can't infinitely respawn their bones (assuming you're talking about shooting bones). They might regenerate during your daysleep due to vampiric stasis, but you would still be pretty limited in ammo, and I'd probably require it to cost extra Vitae like healing if I was the Storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T14:03:04-07:00","id":1550174,"title":"","content":"As a rule of thumb, it's good to stick to preexisting powers and cosmetics when it comes to self alterations, although Horrid Form isn't a bad combat transformation.<br /> <br /> Most of what you'll get out of Vicissitude in most tables is about changing others, not yourself. You can play around with your ghouls, craft objects out of human tissue and so on.<br /> <br /> Turning your arm into a blade is certainly within reach, but you can also directly attack with Vicissitude, impaling the target with their own bones, and that's maybe better than a sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-17T04:21:28-07:00","id":1550208,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude is one of my favourite disciplines because of how open it is to player creativity, and I tend to enjoy exploring bodily augmentation and transhumanism within games. However, it's chief weakness is also that it is so broad and poorly defined, what your character will be capable of will vary wildly between GMs. The easy limits to remember is that it covers the alteration of the human body, flesh, sinew, fat. bone and all that good stuff. You are still limited by the subjects available tissues without learning elder powers, I usually rule the blood expenditure is a mixture of meysphor8cslly wetting the clay and transforming existing flesh or blood between states so bigger projects will either requite external sources for grafts or large amounts of blood. I'd also expect players to pay for attributes or advantages gained, perhaps with a discount. There was a good third party system for it on the Storytellers vault. Another rhing to condider is think of how things would mechanically have to work, mouth hands might need whole new arrangements of flesh and bone to incorporate connections to your gullet and muscles to make them work. Transformed ghouls and people still need their organs to live, still need feeding etc.<br /> finally, a good rule of thumb another poster came up with here some time ago was the &quot;duct tape&quot; rule: can you accomplish the task by taping a piece of mundane equipment to yourself? And thus run these augmentations as if they were freaky mundane equipment, within reason (no vampire fangs don't magically continue to do agg when you move or disconnect them, a common player belief in my circles.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T02:53:56-07:00","id":1550236,"title":"","content":"The problem with using Vicissitude in combat is that it takes a combat system designed to be abstract and tries to make it concrete.<br /> Also what Kale said is very true, it is up to a GM how they treat Vicissitude<br /> <br /> For example, I follow the &quot;Clay in the hands of the sculptor&quot; situation<br /> Just immagine a sculptor in anger simply slaps her creation, a head made out of clay... what will happen that face? It become disfigured and easly ends the fight when the opponent's face become a Picasso painting from his later years after a bottle of wine and some mind altering substance<br /> The sheere horror is enough to induce Frenzy or even <i>R\u00f6tschreck</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kale Fangblade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550103-vicissitude-questions?p=1550208#post1550208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(no vampire fangs don't magically continue to do agg when you move or disconnect them, a common player belief in my circles.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are right<br /> Vicissitude does not inherently have any mystical properties, and the bones of vampires do not inherently have any such properties, so any weapons made with it cause only lethal damage, without something like Thaumaturgy or Koldunic Sorcery to supplement it.<br /> You can use Vicissitude to create weapons out of your own bones and such but don\u2019t expect them to be any good. A spike made out of bone is\u2026 well durable like a bone.<br /> <br /> However, you CAN make bone denser, more durable and a Szalchta with serrated arm blades tough as steel is very dangerous, but still not aggravated. It is more like the shock vallue and of course the terrible wound; gutted by such thing even would make a Vampire's unlife very uncomfortable<br /> <br /> The fangs and claws are a different metter on the other hand. A vampire's bite is agravated like protean claws.<br /> What will happen if you tear them out with Vicissitude or, well, simply by force?<br /> I would say unless you somehow preserve them they<br /> A, dust away or age quickly likie a Cainite's body would do uppon Final Death<br /> B, quickly return to normal; both the Claws and Fangs require effort to &quot;summon&quot;, unless you have a flaw your fangs are always out (just don't bite your tounge... agaravated, ouch) your normal bite is quite a blount one. But the editions and systems never really were clear in this matter.<br /> Vampires can cause aggravated damage naturally only if they use their teeth...somehow. I'm not sure there is really a satisfactory description for how that really works but if you bite down using normal teeth, that's blunt damage (often not even causing damage), if you use the vampiric fangs as an attack, it's aggravated.<br /> So I tend to treat this as the Garou transforming back to its breed from, like their bodyparts if something tear it off; a big bad Crinos arm become a human arm or a wolf paw (unless it was a metis) like how you will not have a Crinois trophy-head any time soon (again unless it was a Metis). A dead Garou will be a dead human body or a dead wolf body.<br /> Following this, unless you soemhow with a ritual preserve it, you will have a normal tooth or nails if you tear them out from a vampire. At least untill they dust/rot away. There are of course Vampire artefact like the Femur of Toompler, but they are exeptions not rules. Similar with a Gangrel's fangs in wolf-form, yank them out they will return to normal<br /> At least in my interpretation... other GM? Who know?<br /> <br /> Of course you can make weapons out of your body but that needs a combination discipline, Body Armory. In V20 you can find it in Lore of the Clans page 241.<br /> <br /> &quot;This power enables the vampire to form wicked weapons from her own body. The vampire may create sword blades, axes, and even spiked mauls. These weapons do terrible damage to their targets. Many Tzimisce make sword-arms, knife-bladed knuckles, and the like, but more dramatic implementations are possible.<br /> <br /> System: This power costs two blood points per weapon (though larger weapons like two-handed swords and great axes cost four), and the player must roll Dexterity + Medicine (difficulty 7). Each weapon takes two turns to form (larger weapons take three turns). Weapons created in this manner cause aggravated damage.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nice and simple<br /> Similarly there is a wicked combat application of Vicissitude<br /> <br /> Flaying Touch<br /> (Potence \u2022\u2022, Vicissitude \u2022\u2022)<br /> A Tzimisce can tear away a victim\u2019s skin as easily as removing a robe, The Fiend simply grabs a handful of skin and pulls it away. The target suffers excruciating pain and begins bleeding, and even if a target somehow survives the blood loss, the area of skinless flesh soon becomes infected. Even Cainites suffer under this agony, though they do not have to fear blood loss.\u200b<br /> <br /> But it literally tears off the skin in a spectacular fashion; again it is more of the shock vallue than the damage itself<br /> <br /> Herophilus of Chalcedon discovered and proved the existence of the Nervous System around 300 BC<br /> This is important, because most of the Tzimisce 4th Gen were Embraced around 8000 BC, if you belive the clan legends, before the flood and were master pacticioners of Vicissitude, proving you don't really need deep and academic knowledge how the hell the body works to alter it<br /> Probably they formulated some theories and there is that cute little level 6 power called:<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 \u2022 Ecstatic Agony<br /> <br /> Pain is transformative. Pain awakens primal potential in the tortured flesh. A Fiend with this ability delights in every slash of the blade and caress of bullet, transmogrifying agony into physical prowess and incredible displays of Caine\u2019s Gifts.<br /> <b>System:</b> After spending two Willpower points, the character becomes empowered by pain. Add his wound penalties to all non-reflexive actions involving a Physical Attribute or use of a Discipline. As the character heals, this bonus wanes. Treat Incapacitated and Final Death normally. This power lasts for one scene.<br /> <br /> So by sheer willpower and Vicissitude you basically fine tune your nervous system?<br /> It never really was explained in detail<br /> <br /> It is an age old debate among Tzimisce fans a Fiend well versed in the art of neurology and anatomy and everything that studies the Body what could do with Vicissitude (the Clanbook even mentioned some efforts to ghoul bacteria and other nasty implications of bio-weapons)<br /> Or even how the blood vesseles and nervous system <i>behaves </i>while you craft your new Szlachta or couch made out of a Hunter who had a bad day (and will have many more worse days)<br /> <br /> At the end of the day when it comes to Vicissitude there are tow basic advice:<br /> - Be creative<br /> - Talk it over with your GM what and how she allows because in the past three decades or so no two GM managed to treat Vicissitude and its applicitons the same way<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-18-2025, 06:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T11:06:02-07:00","id":1550244,"title":"","content":"I don't thing vampire fangs would revert to normal upon death. Garou are shapeshifters, that's a whole another thing, they're about metaphysics and spirituality. Vampires are about physicality and stasis. Also, WtA is strongly about the idea of being cut-off from humanity in a way that humans won't ever bear witness to your fights, for good or ill. VtM is strongly about going out of your way to clean the evidence of your existence.<br /> <br /> And the game does say vampire fangs cause Agg because supernatural. A removed fang simply ceases to be supernatural, even if it doesn't crumble. For me, it would retain the form and size it acquired upon the Embrace, clearly inhuman. And it should remain mostly intact.<br /> <br /> Teeth are the body part that's most resilient to the passage of time, and the crumbling into dust in this game is about the body undergoing decay <i><b>until it reaches its true age</b></i>. Young vampires shouldn't become actual dust, vestiges of bones should be in most &quot;dusted&quot; vampires, and teeth remaining should be a common thing, specially if removed with Vicissitude instead of pulled by force alone or collected from a killed vampire.<br /> <br /> Clean after yourself. Don't count on &quot;dusting&quot; being an automatic elimination of evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-18T13:18:13-07:00","id":1550246,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> That is why I wrote dust/rot away - depend on the age<br /> <br /> And as I said, depends on the GM<br /> <br /> A tetusbo-like weapon but instead of iron nails adorend with vampire fangs sounds and looks scary, but while a human teeth tend to survive well, some for tens of thousands of years and actually after death there is little or nothing to cause them to decay unless they are in a very acid environment, and even then they take a long time to dissolve, a tooth is not that strong.<br /> While they are not necessarily decay, a tooth brake and chip easily<br /> It is more like in my opinion a vampire fang would revert back to a normal sized human blunt canine.<br /> <br /> Supernatural or not, the vampire bite is not clearly defined<br /> Only your fangs are supernatural and cause agaravated? All of your teeth are?<br /> Biting the hand someone, like in a kindergarten yard fight <i>without </i>growing your tiny human canines in to sharp fangs cause agravated? Or just simple not even bruised?<br /> I thin kthey even limited you always do exactly 2 aggravated damage with a successful bite... but to be honest it is more of a faint memory than a fact<br /> <br /> My point is, after a Sabbat siege and their mass embraced/destroyed shovelheads a Prince would have a bunch of bodies with vampire fangs to deal with, or even a handfull of lying around<br /> And usually it is not the case, maybe just downplayed maybe people rearly think about it, but I think - and I could be very worng - simply because the vampire body just like how it reverts back to the moment of Embrace, after Final Death reverts back to a human corpse too, including but not limited to removed body parts or torn out fangs and claws<br /> Even after a proper cremation most of the teeth survives and while it is amusing to think about the logistic and the lenght a Prince have to go to get rid of such evidance I don't think this is the case simply because no evidance remains juts human coprses with human teeths and nails<br /> <br /> But again I could be wrong<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-20T13:24:57-07:00","id":1550290,"title":"","content":"Precisely because there's no mentions of those details in the rules, it's a matter of preference.<br /> <br /> I don't personally think that reverting the canines upon death combines with the themes and tropes of the game. Same way as I think only the canines are mystic weapons, but if suddenly comes a situation where you think every teeth being Agg dealers makes for a better story, go for it.<br /> <br /> But as far as corpses go: leaving corpses behind is generally a bad idea, specially if they're vampire corpses. Even the &quot;fresh&quot; corpses of shovelheads or other fledglings will be decayed by hours or days more than they should, possibly showing marks of death causes that shouldn't exist, and while WoD's police isn't very effective, taking chances doesn't make for a long life. Cleaning up the bodies should be a regular, expected work when violence escalates enough for vampires to suffer Final Death. In such a circumstance, cleaning teeth is more of a curiosity than a game changing work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}